-- ccc29-xxviii-3-peace-810-21.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), PART XXVII, "Sureties to Keep the Peace": sections 810.21 (audioconference or videoconference),
-- 810.22 (transfer of order), 810.3 (samples: designations and specifications), 810.4 (prohibition on use of a bodily substance),
-- 810.5 (orders under sections 486 to 486.5 and 486.7), 811 (breach of recognizance) and 811.1 (proof of certificate of analyst).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. The text is a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation
-- (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text. The conventions of ccc29-xxviii-0-peace-810.l4 apply unchanged.
-- "810 to 810.2" is read in the Code's own order, which includes sections 810.01, 810.011, 810.02, 810.03 and 810.1 (fork F-810.21-1).

§ `Section 810.21 -- Audioconference or videoconference`

-- 810.21(1) If a defendant is required to appear under any of sections 83.3 and 810 to 810.2, a provincial court judge may, on application of the prosecutor, order that the defendant appear by audioconference or videoconference.
-- src:17055 | Audioconference or videoconference
-- src:17056 | 810.21 (1) If a defendant is required to appear under any of sections 83.3 and 810 to 810.2, a provincial court judge may, on application of the prosecutor, order that the defendant appear by audioconference or videoconference.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.21(1) (src:17055-17056)
GIVEN `the number of the section under which the defendant is required to appear` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 810.21(1) the section is one of 83.3 and 810 to 810.2` MEANS
    `the number of the section under which the defendant is required to appear` EQUALS 83.3
    OR (`the number of the section under which the defendant is required to appear` AT LEAST 810 AND `the number of the section under which the defendant is required to appear` AT MOST 810.2)

@ref Criminal Code s 810.21(1) (src:17055-17056)
-- @name-test: flipped to NOTHING AND listed, where/when/upon kind (F-810.21-1): "If a defendant is required to appear" answers NOTHING; "on application of the prosecutor" answers JUST FALSE
GIVEN `the number of the section under which the defendant is required to appear` IS A NUMBER
      `the prosecutor applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.21(1) a provincial court judge may order that the defendant appear by audioconference or videoconference` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 810.21(1) the section is one of 83.3 and 810 to 810.2` `the number of the section under which the defendant is required to appear`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a defendant is required to appear under any of sections 83.3 and 810 to 810.2"
        IF NOT `the prosecutor applies` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on application of the prosecutor"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 810.21(2) Despite section 769, sections 714.1 to 714.8 and Part XXII.01 apply, with any necessary modifications, to proceedings under this section.
-- src:17058 | (2) Despite section 769, sections 714.1 to 714.8 and Part XXII.01 apply, with any necessary modifications, to proceedings under this section.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.21(2) (src:17058)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings under section 810.21` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.21(2) sections 714.1 to 714.8 and Part XXII.01 apply to the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are proceedings under section 810.21`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to proceedings under this section"

§ `Section 810.22 -- Transfer of order`

-- 810.22(1) If a person who is bound by an order under any of sections 83.3 and 810 to 810.2 becomes a resident of -- or is charged with, convicted of or discharged under section 730 of an offence, including an offence under section 811, in -- a territorial division other than the territorial division in which the order was made, on application of a peace officer or the Attorney General, a provincial court judge may, subject to subsection (2), transfer the order to a provincial court judge in that other territorial division and the order may then be dealt with and enforced by the provincial court judge to whom it is transferred in all respects as if that provincial court judge had made the order.
-- src:17059 | Transfer of order
-- src:17060 | 810.22 (1) If a person who is bound by an order under any of sections 83.3 and 810 to 810.2 becomes a resident of — or is charged with, convicted of or discharged under section 730 of an offence, including an offence under section 811, in — a territorial division other than the territorial division in which the order was made, on application of a peace officer or the Attorney General, a provincial court judge may, subject to subsection (2), transfer the order to a provincial court judge in that other territorial division and the order may then be dealt with and enforced by the provincial court judge to whom it is transferred in all respects as if that provincial court judge had made the order.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.22(1) (src:17059-17060)
-- @name-test: flipped to NOTHING AND listed, where/when/upon kind (F-810.22-1): "If a person who is bound ... becomes a resident ..." answers NOTHING; "on application of a peace officer or the Attorney General" answers JUST FALSE
GIVEN `the number of the section under which the order was made` IS A NUMBER
      `the person becomes a resident of a territorial division other than the one in which the order was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is charged with, convicted of or discharged under section 730 of an offence in a territorial division other than the one in which the order was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a peace officer applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.22(1) a provincial court judge may transfer the order to a provincial court judge in the other territorial division` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 810.21(1) the section is one of 83.3 and 810 to 810.2` `the number of the section under which the order was made`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person who is bound by an order under any of sections 83.3 and 810 to 810.2"
        IF NOT (`the person becomes a resident of a territorial division other than the one in which the order was made` OR `the person is charged with, convicted of or discharged under section 730 of an offence in a territorial division other than the one in which the order was made`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "becomes a resident of -- or is charged with, convicted of or discharged under section 730 of an offence ... in -- a territorial division other than the territorial division in which the order was made"
        IF NOT (`a peace officer applies` OR `the Attorney General applies`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on application of a peace officer or the Attorney General"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 810.22(2) The transfer may be granted only with (a) the consent of the Attorney General of the province in which the order was made, if the two territorial divisions are not in the same province; or (b) the consent of the Attorney General of Canada, if the information that led to the issuance of the order was laid with the consent of the Attorney General of Canada.
-- src:17061 | Attorney General’s consent
-- src:17062 | (2) The transfer may be granted only with
-- src:17063 | (a) the consent of the Attorney General of the province in which the order was made, if the two territorial divisions are not in the same province; or
-- src:17064 | (b) the consent of the Attorney General of Canada, if the information that led to the issuance of the order was laid with the consent of the Attorney General of Canada.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.22(2) to s 810.22(2)(b) (src:17061-17064)
-- Fork F-810.22-2: read as alternatives, one consent suffices; read as cases, each consent is required where its own "if" holds. The part takes the second reading (cumulative), and answers NOTHING where neither "if" holds.
GIVEN `the two territorial divisions are not in the same province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General of the province in which the order was made consents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information that led to the issuance of the order was laid with the consent of the Attorney General of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General of Canada consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.22(2) the transfer is barred for want of the consent that the subsection requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the two territorial divisions are not in the same province` OR `the information that led to the issuance of the order was laid with the consent of the Attorney General of Canada`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): neither paragraph (a) nor paragraph (b) names a consent for this case
        IF `the two territorial divisions are not in the same province` AND NOT `the Attorney General of the province in which the order was made consents` THEN JUST TRUE   -- the transfer "may be granted only with" the consent in (a)
        IF `the information that led to the issuance of the order was laid with the consent of the Attorney General of Canada` AND NOT `the Attorney General of Canada consents` THEN JUST TRUE   -- the transfer "may be granted only with" the consent in (b)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The transfer may be granted only with"

-- 810.22(3) If the judge who made the order or a judge to whom an order has been transferred is for any reason unable to act, the powers of that judge in relation to the order may be exercised by any other judge of the same court.
-- src:17065 | If judge unable to act
-- src:17066 | (3) If the judge who made the order or a judge to whom an order has been transferred is for any reason unable to act, the powers of that judge in relation to the order may be exercised by any other judge of the same court.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.22(3) (src:17065-17066)
-- @name-test: flipped to NOTHING; gate "If the judge ... is for any reason unable to act" (fork F-810.22-3)
GIVEN `the judge who made the order or a judge to whom an order has been transferred is for any reason unable to act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other judge is a judge of the same court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.22(3) the powers of the judge in relation to the order may be exercised by another judge of the same court` MEANS
    IF `the judge who made the order or a judge to whom an order has been transferred is for any reason unable to act` AND `the other judge is a judge of the same court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the judge ... is for any reason unable to act, the powers ... may be exercised by any other judge of the same court"

§ `Section 810.3 -- Samples: designations and specifications`

-- 810.3(1) For the purposes of sections 810, 810.01, 810.03, 810.011, 810.1 and 810.2 and subject to the regulations, the Attorney General of a province or the minister of justice of a territory shall, with respect to the province or territory, (a) designate the persons or classes of persons that may take samples of bodily substances; (b) designate the places or classes of places at which the samples are to be taken; (c) specify the manner in which the samples are to be taken; (d) specify the manner in which the samples are to be analyzed; (e) specify the manner in which the samples are to be stored, handled and destroyed; (f) specify the manner in which the records of the results of the analysis of the samples are to be protected and destroyed; (g) designate the persons or classes of persons that may destroy the samples; and (h) designate the persons or classes of persons that may destroy the records of the results of the analysis of the samples.
-- src:17067 | Samples — designations and specifications
-- src:17068 | 810.3 (1) For the purposes of sections 810, 810.01, 810.03, 810.011, 810.1 and 810.2 and subject to the regulations, the Attorney General of a province or the minister of justice of a territory shall, with respect to the province or territory,
-- src:17069 | (a) designate the persons or classes of persons that may take samples of bodily substances;
-- src:17070 | (b) designate the places or classes of places at which the samples are to be taken;
-- src:17071 | (c) specify the manner in which the samples are to be taken;
-- src:17072 | (d) specify the manner in which the samples are to be analyzed;
-- src:17073 | (e) specify the manner in which the samples are to be stored, handled and destroyed;
-- src:17074 | (f) specify the manner in which the records of the results of the analysis of the samples are to be protected and destroyed;
-- src:17075 | (g) designate the persons or classes of persons that may destroy the samples; and
-- src:17076 | (h) designate the persons or classes of persons that may destroy the records of the results of the analysis of the samples.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.3(1) to s 810.3(1)(h) (src:17067-17076)
DECLARE `s 810.3 designating authority` IS ONE OF
    `s 810.3 the Attorney General of a province`
    `s 810.3 the minister of justice of a territory`
    `s 810.3 a person authorized by the Attorney General or minister`

DECLARE `s 810.3(1) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 810.3(1)(a) designate the persons or classes of persons that may take samples of bodily substances`
    `s 810.3(1)(b) designate the places or classes of places at which the samples are to be taken`
    `s 810.3(1)(c) specify the manner in which the samples are to be taken`
    `s 810.3(1)(d) specify the manner in which the samples are to be analyzed`
    `s 810.3(1)(e) specify the manner in which the samples are to be stored, handled and destroyed`
    `s 810.3(1)(f) specify the manner in which the records of the results of the analysis of the samples are to be protected and destroyed`
    `s 810.3(1)(g) designate the persons or classes of persons that may destroy the samples`
    `s 810.3(1)(h) designate the persons or classes of persons that may destroy the records of the results of the analysis of the samples`
    `s 810.3(1) another matter`

DECLARE `s 810.3 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 810.3(1) designate or specify the matter` HAS matter IS A `s 810.3(1) matter`
    `s 810.3(4) cause the samples to be destroyed`

@ref Criminal Code s 810.3(1) (src:17067-17068)
GIVEN `the section is one of 810, 810.01, 810.03, 810.011, 810.1 and 810.2` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `s 810.3(1) matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.3(1) the authority is required to designate or specify the matter` MEANS
    IF `the section is one of 810, 810.01, 810.03, 810.011, 810.1 and 810.2`
    THEN CONSIDER matter
         WHEN `s 810.3(1)(a) designate the persons or classes of persons that may take samples of bodily substances` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.3(1)(b) designate the places or classes of places at which the samples are to be taken` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.3(1)(c) specify the manner in which the samples are to be taken` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.3(1)(d) specify the manner in which the samples are to be analyzed` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.3(1)(e) specify the manner in which the samples are to be stored, handled and destroyed` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.3(1)(f) specify the manner in which the records of the results of the analysis of the samples are to be protected and destroyed` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.3(1)(g) designate the persons or classes of persons that may destroy the samples` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.3(1)(h) designate the persons or classes of persons that may destroy the records of the results of the analysis of the samples` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.3(1) another matter` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names eight matters and no other
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of sections 810, 810.01, 810.03, 810.011, 810.1 and 810.2"

@ref Criminal Code s 810.3(1) (src:17067-17068)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 810.3 designating authority` `s 810.3 action`
`s 810.3(1) the authority is to designate or specify the matter` MEANS
    PARTY `s 810.3 the Attorney General of a province`
    MUST `s 810.3(1) designate or specify the matter` matter

-- 810.3(2) Subject to the regulations, the Attorney General of a province or the minister of justice of a territory may, with respect to the province or territory, designate the persons or classes of persons (a) to make a demand for a sample of a bodily substance for the purposes of paragraphs 810(3.02)(b), 810.01(4.1)(f), 810.011(6)(e), 810.03(7)(g), 810.1(3.02)(h) and 810.2(4.1)(f); and (b) to specify the regular intervals at which a defendant must provide a sample of a bodily substance for the purposes of paragraphs 810(3.02)(c), 810.01(4.1)(g), 810.011(6)(f), 810.03(7)(h), 810.1(3.02)(i) and 810.2(4.1)(g).
-- src:17077 | Further designations
-- src:17078 | (2) Subject to the regulations, the Attorney General of a province or the minister of justice of a territory may, with respect to the province or territory, designate the persons or classes of persons
-- src:17079 | (a) to make a demand for a sample of a bodily substance for the purposes of paragraphs 810(3.02)(b), 810.01(4.1)(f), 810.011(6)(e), 810.03(7)(g), 810.1(3.02)(h) and 810.2(4.1)(f); and
-- src:17080 | (b) to specify the regular intervals at which a defendant must provide a sample of a bodily substance for the purposes of paragraphs 810(3.02)(c), 810.01(4.1)(g), 810.011(6)(f), 810.03(7)(h), 810.1(3.02)(i) and 810.2(4.1)(g).
@ref Criminal Code s 810.3(2) to s 810.3(2)(b) (src:17077-17080)
DECLARE `s 810.3(2) designation` IS ONE OF
    `s 810.3(2)(a) designate the persons or classes of persons to make a demand for a sample of a bodily substance`
    `s 810.3(2)(b) designate the persons or classes of persons to specify the regular intervals at which a defendant must provide a sample`
    `s 810.3(2) another designation`

@ref Criminal Code s 810.3(2) (src:17077-17078)
-- @name-test: no JUST FALSE branch; named for a power, answers NOTHING outside the two designations
GIVEN designation IS A `s 810.3(2) designation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.3(2) the authority may make the designation` MEANS
    CONSIDER designation
    WHEN `s 810.3(2)(a) designate the persons or classes of persons to make a demand for a sample of a bodily substance` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 810.3(2)(b) designate the persons or classes of persons to specify the regular intervals at which a defendant must provide a sample` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 810.3(2) another designation` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "designate the persons or classes of persons (a) ... and (b) ..."

-- 810.3(3) Samples of bodily substances referred to in sections 810, 810.01, 810.011, 810.03, 810.1 and 810.2 may not be taken, analyzed, stored, handled or destroyed, and the records of the results of the analysis of the samples may not be protected or destroyed, except in accordance with the designations and specifications made under subsection (1).
-- src:17081 | Restriction
-- src:17082 | (3) Samples of bodily substances referred to in sections 810, 810.01, 810.011, 810.03, 810.1 and 810.2 may not be taken, analyzed, stored, handled or destroyed, and the records of the results of the analysis of the samples may not be protected or destroyed, except in accordance with the designations and specifications made under subsection (1).
@ref Criminal Code s 810.3(3) (src:17081-17082)
GIVEN `the samples are samples of bodily substances referred to in sections 810, 810.01, 810.011, 810.03, 810.1 and 810.2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sample or record is dealt with in accordance with the designations and specifications made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.3(3) the taking, analysis, storage, handling or destruction of the sample, or the protection or destruction of the record, is barred` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the samples are samples of bodily substances referred to in sections 810, 810.01, 810.011, 810.03, 810.1 and 810.2` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Samples of bodily substances referred to in sections 810, 810.01, 810.011, 810.03, 810.1 and 810.2"
        IF `the sample or record is dealt with in accordance with the designations and specifications made under subsection (1)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except in accordance with the designations and specifications made under subsection (1)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 810.3(4) The Attorney General of a province or the minister of justice of a territory, or a person authorized by the Attorney General or minister, shall cause all samples of bodily substances provided under a recognizance under section 810, 810.01, 810.011, 810.03, 810.1 or 810.2 to be destroyed within the period prescribed by regulation unless the samples are reasonably expected to be used as evidence in a proceeding for an offence under section 811.
-- src:17083 | Destruction of samples
-- src:17084 | (4) The Attorney General of a province or the minister of justice of a territory, or a person authorized by the Attorney General or minister, shall cause all samples of bodily substances provided under a recognizance under section 810, 810.01, 810.011, 810.03, 810.1 or 810.2 to be destroyed within the period prescribed by regulation unless the samples are reasonably expected to be used as evidence in a proceeding for an offence under section 811.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.3(4) (src:17083-17084)
-- Fork F-810.3(4): the period is "prescribed by regulation" (outside these sources) and the text does not say when it starts, so no deadline is encoded; the duty is.
GIVEN `the samples were provided under a recognizance under section 810, 810.01, 810.011, 810.03, 810.1 or 810.2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the samples are reasonably expected to be used as evidence in a proceeding for an offence under section 811` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.3(4) the authority is required to cause the samples to be destroyed within the period prescribed by regulation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the samples were provided under a recognizance under section 810, 810.01, 810.011, 810.03, 810.1 or 810.2` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "all samples of bodily substances provided under a recognizance under section 810, 810.01, 810.011, 810.03, 810.1 or 810.2"
        IF `the samples are reasonably expected to be used as evidence in a proceeding for an offence under section 811` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the samples are reasonably expected to be used as evidence in a proceeding for an offence under section 811"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref Criminal Code s 810.3(4) (src:17083-17084)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 810.3 designating authority` `s 810.3 action`
`s 810.3(4) the authority is to cause the samples to be destroyed` MEANS
    PARTY `s 810.3 the Attorney General of a province`
    MUST `s 810.3(4) cause the samples to be destroyed`

-- 810.3(5) The Governor in Council may make regulations (a) prescribing bodily substances ...; (b) respecting the designations and specifications referred to in subsections (1) and (2); (c) prescribing the periods within which samples of bodily substances are to be destroyed under subsection (4); and (d) respecting any other matters relating to the samples of bodily substances.
-- Not encoded (a regulation-making power: machinery, inert reason 2 of the brief). The amounts and periods it leaves open are inputs wherever the text above asks for them.

-- 810.3(6) The notice referred to in paragraph 810(3.02)(c), 810.01(4.1)(g), 810.011(6)(f), 810.03(7)(h), 810.1(3.02)(i) or 810.2(4.1)(g) must specify the places and times at which and the days on which the defendant must provide samples of a bodily substance under a condition described in that paragraph. The first sample may not be taken earlier than 24 hours after the defendant is served with the notice, and subsequent samples must be taken at regular intervals of at least seven days.
-- src:17091 | Notice — samples at regular intervals
-- src:17092 | (6) The notice referred to in paragraph 810(3.02)(c), 810.01(4.1)(g), 810.011(6)(f), 810.03(7)(h), 810.1(3.02)(i) or 810.2(4.1)(g) must specify the places and times at which and the days on which the defendant must provide samples of a bodily substance under a condition described in that paragraph. The first sample may not be taken earlier than 24 hours after the defendant is served with the notice, and subsequent samples must be taken at regular intervals of at least seven days.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.3(6) (src:17091-17092)
GIVEN `it is the notice referred to in paragraph 810(3.02)(c), 810.01(4.1)(g), 810.011(6)(f), 810.03(7)(h), 810.1(3.02)(i) or 810.2(4.1)(g)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.3(6) the notice is required to specify the places and times at which and the days on which the defendant must provide samples` MEANS
    IF `it is the notice referred to in paragraph 810(3.02)(c), 810.01(4.1)(g), 810.011(6)(f), 810.03(7)(h), 810.1(3.02)(i) or 810.2(4.1)(g)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The notice referred to in paragraph 810(3.02)(c), 810.01(4.1)(g), 810.011(6)(f), 810.03(7)(h), 810.1(3.02)(i) or 810.2(4.1)(g)"

@ref Criminal Code s 810.3(6) (src:17091-17092)
GIVEN `the hours between service of the notice and the first sample` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.3(6) the first sample is barred because it is taken earlier than 24 hours after the defendant is served with the notice` MEANS
    IF `the hours between service of the notice and the first sample` AT LEAST 24
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The first sample may not be taken earlier than 24 hours after the defendant is served with the notice"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref Criminal Code s 810.3(6) (src:17091-17092)
GIVEN `the days between one sample and the next` IS A NUMBER
      `the intervals are regular` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.3(6) the subsequent samples are taken at regular intervals of at least seven days` MEANS
    IF `the intervals are regular` AND `the days between one sample and the next` AT LEAST 7
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subsequent samples must be taken at regular intervals of at least seven days"

§ `Section 810.4 -- Prohibition on use of a bodily substance`

-- 810.4(1) No person shall use a bodily substance provided under a recognizance under section 810, 810.01, 810.011, 810.03, 810.1 or 810.2 except for the purpose of determining whether a defendant is complying with a condition in the recognizance that they abstain from the consumption of drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance.
-- src:17093 | Prohibition on use of bodily substance
-- src:17094 | 810.4 (1) No person shall use a bodily substance provided under a recognizance under section 810, 810.01, 810.011, 810.03, 810.1 or 810.2 except for the purpose of determining whether a defendant is complying with a condition in the recognizance that they abstain from the consumption of drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.4(1) (src:17093-17094)
GIVEN `the bodily substance was provided under a recognizance under section 810, 810.01, 810.011, 810.03, 810.1 or 810.2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is used for the purpose of determining whether a defendant is complying with a condition in the recognizance that they abstain from the consumption of drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.4(1) the use of the bodily substance is barred` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the bodily substance was provided under a recognizance under section 810, 810.01, 810.011, 810.03, 810.1 or 810.2` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a bodily substance provided under a recognizance under section 810, 810.01, 810.011, 810.03, 810.1 or 810.2"
        IF `it is used for the purpose of determining whether a defendant is complying with a condition in the recognizance that they abstain from the consumption of drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except for the purpose of determining whether a defendant is complying with a condition"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 810.4(2) Subject to subsection (3), no person shall use, disclose or allow the disclosure of the results of the analysis of a bodily substance provided under a recognizance under section 810, 810.01, 810.011, 810.03, 810.1 or 810.2.
-- src:17095 | Prohibition on use or disclosure of result
-- src:17096 | (2) Subject to subsection (3), no person shall use, disclose or allow the disclosure of the results of the analysis of a bodily substance provided under a recognizance under section 810, 810.01, 810.011, 810.03, 810.1 or 810.2.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.4(2) (src:17095-17096)
GIVEN `the results are the results of the analysis of a bodily substance provided under a recognizance under section 810, 810.01, 810.011, 810.03, 810.1 or 810.2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use or disclosure is one that subsection (3) allows, by s 810.4(3) the results may be disclosed or used` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.4(2) the use or disclosure of the results of the analysis is barred` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the results are the results of the analysis of a bodily substance provided under a recognizance under section 810, 810.01, 810.011, 810.03, 810.1 or 810.2` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the results of the analysis of a bodily substance provided under a recognizance under section 810, 810.01, 810.011, 810.03, 810.1 or 810.2"
        IF `the use or disclosure is one that subsection (3) allows, by s 810.4(3) the results may be disclosed or used` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsection (3)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- the bar is a flat negative: "no person shall use, disclose or allow the disclosure"; where subsection (3) is silent the bar stands

-- 810.4(3) The results of the analysis of a bodily substance provided under a recognizance under section 810, 810.01, 810.011, 810.03, 810.1 or 810.2 may be disclosed to the defendant to whom they relate, and may also be used or disclosed in the course of an investigation of, or in a proceeding for, an offence under section 811 or, if the results are made anonymous, for statistical or other research purposes.
-- src:17097 | Exception
-- src:17098 | (3) The results of the analysis of a bodily substance provided under a recognizance under section 810, 810.01, 810.011, 810.03, 810.1 or 810.2 may be disclosed to the defendant to whom they relate, and may also be used or disclosed in the course of an investigation of, or in a proceeding for, an offence under section 811 or, if the results are made anonymous, for statistical or other research purposes.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.4(3) (src:17097-17098)
DECLARE `s 810.4(3) use or disclosure` IS ONE OF
    `s 810.4(3) disclosure to the defendant to whom the results relate`
    `s 810.4(3) use or disclosure in the course of an investigation of an offence under section 811`
    `s 810.4(3) use or disclosure in a proceeding for an offence under section 811`
    `s 810.4(3) use or disclosure for statistical or other research purposes`
    `s 810.4(3) another use or disclosure`

@ref Criminal Code s 810.4(3) (src:17097-17098)
-- @name-test: flipped to NOTHING; gate "if the results are made anonymous" for the research limb (fork F-810.4-3)
GIVEN use IS A `s 810.4(3) use or disclosure`
      `the results are made anonymous` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.4(3) the results may be disclosed or used` MEANS
    CONSIDER use
    WHEN `s 810.4(3) disclosure to the defendant to whom the results relate` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 810.4(3) use or disclosure in the course of an investigation of an offence under section 811` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 810.4(3) use or disclosure in a proceeding for an offence under section 811` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 810.4(3) use or disclosure for statistical or other research purposes` THEN IF `the results are made anonymous` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the results are made anonymous, for statistical or other research purposes"
    WHEN `s 810.4(3) another use or disclosure` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may also be used or disclosed"

-- 810.4(4) Every person who contravenes subsection (1) or (2) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
-- src:17099 | Offence
-- src:17100 | (4) Every person who contravenes subsection (1) or (2) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.4(4) (src:17099-17100)
GIVEN `the person contravenes subsection (1), by s 810.4(1) the use of the bodily substance is barred` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person contravenes subsection (2), by s 810.4(2) the use or disclosure of the results of the analysis is barred` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.4(4) the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person contravenes subsection (1), by s 810.4(1) the use of the bodily substance is barred` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person contravenes subsection (2), by s 810.4(2) the use or disclosure of the results of the analysis is barred` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person contravenes subsection (1), by s 810.4(1) the use of the bodily substance is barred` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `the person contravenes subsection (2), by s 810.4(2) the use or disclosure of the results of the analysis is barred` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who contravenes subsection (1) or (2) is guilty"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer rests on the section 810.4(1) or (2) answer, which is itself "not covered"

@ref Criminal Code s 810.4(4) (src:17099-17100)
-- The text names no penalty for this offence: it is "punishable on summary conviction", so the general penalty of section 787(1) applies unless the law otherwise provides (fork F-810.4-4).
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 810.4(4) the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    `s 787(1) the general penalty as stated in section 787(1)`

§ `Section 810.5 -- Orders under sections 486 to 486.5 and 486.7`

-- 810.5(1) Sections 486 to 486.5 and 486.7 apply, with any necessary modifications, to proceedings under any of sections 83.3 and 810 to 810.2.
-- src:17101 | Orders under sections 486 to 486.5 and 486.7
-- src:17102 | 810.5 (1) Sections 486 to 486.5 and 486.7 apply, with any necessary modifications, to proceedings under any of sections 83.3 and 810 to 810.2.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.5(1) (src:17101-17102)
GIVEN `the number of the section under which the proceedings are taken` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.5(1) sections 486 to 486.5 and 486.7 apply to the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `s 810.21(1) the section is one of 83.3 and 810 to 810.2` `the number of the section under which the proceedings are taken`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to proceedings under any of sections 83.3 and 810 to 810.2"

-- 810.5(2) Every person who fails to comply with an order made under any of subsections 486.4(1) to (3) or subsection 486.5(1) or (2) in proceedings referred to in subsection (1) is guilty of an offence under section 486.6.
-- src:17103 | Offence — order restricting publication
-- src:17104 | (2) Every person who fails to comply with an order made under any of subsections 486.4(1) to (3) or subsection 486.5(1) or (2) in proceedings referred to in subsection (1) is guilty of an offence under section 486.6.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.5(2) (src:17103-17104)
-- Fork F-810.5-2: "486.4(1) to (3)" is taken as the three subsections named; a range in the Code's order would also take in any subsection numbered between (2) and (3), and the text of this part does not show section 486.4.
GIVEN `the provision under which the order was made` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the order was made in proceedings referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fails to comply with the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.5(2) the person is guilty of an offence under section 486.6` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the order was made in proceedings referred to in subsection (1)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in proceedings referred to in subsection (1)"
        IF NOT (    (`the provision under which the order was made`'s `section` EQUALS 486.4
                     AND (    `the provision under which the order was made`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)"
                           OR `the provision under which the order was made`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(2)"
                           OR `the provision under which the order was made`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(3)" ))
                 OR (`the provision under which the order was made`'s `section` EQUALS 486.5
                     AND (    `the provision under which the order was made`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)"
                           OR `the provision under which the order was made`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(2)" )))
           THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an order made under any of subsections 486.4(1) to (3) or subsection 486.5(1) or (2)"
        IF `the person fails to comply with the order` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who fails to comply with an order"

§ `Section 811 -- Breach of recognizance`

-- 811 A person bound by a recognizance under any of sections 83.3 and 810 to 810.2 who commits a breach of the recognizance is guilty of (a) an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than four years; or (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
-- src:17105 | Breach of recognizance
-- src:17106 | 811 A person bound by a recognizance under any of sections 83.3 and 810 to 810.2 who commits a breach of the recognizance is guilty of
-- src:17107 | (a) an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than four years; or
-- src:17108 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 811 to s 811(b) (src:17105-17108)
GIVEN `the number of the section under which the person is bound by a recognizance` IS A NUMBER
      `the person commits a breach of the recognizance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 811 the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 810.21(1) the section is one of 83.3 and 810 to 810.2` `the number of the section under which the person is bound by a recognizance`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person bound by a recognizance under any of sections 83.3 and 810 to 810.2"
        IF `the person commits a breach of the recognizance` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "who commits a breach of the recognizance is guilty"

@ref Criminal Code s 811 to s 811(b) (src:17105-17108)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 811 the class of the offence` MEANS
    `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 811(a) (src:17107)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 811(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 4, 0, 0, FALSE)), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 811(b) (src:17108)
-- The text names no penalty for limb (b): the general penalty of section 787(1) applies unless the law otherwise provides (fork F-811-b).
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 811(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    `s 787(1) the general penalty as stated in section 787(1)`

§ `Section 811.1 -- Proof of certificate of analyst: bodily substance`

-- 811.1(1) In a prosecution for breach of a condition in a recognizance under section 810, 810.01, 810.011, 810.03, 810.1 or 810.2 that a defendant not consume drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance, a certificate purporting to be signed by an analyst that states that the analyst has analyzed a sample of a bodily substance and that states the result of the analysis is admissible in evidence and, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, is proof of the statements contained in the certificate without proof of the signature or official character of the person who appears to have signed the certificate.
-- src:17109 | Proof of certificate of analyst — bodily substance
-- src:17110 | 811.1 (1) In a prosecution for breach of a condition in a recognizance under section 810, 810.01, 810.011, 810.03, 810.1 or 810.2 that a defendant not consume drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance, a certificate purporting to be signed by an analyst that states that the analyst has analyzed a sample of a bodily substance and that states the result of the analysis is admissible in evidence and, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, is proof of the statements contained in the certificate without proof of the signature or official character of the person who appears to have signed the certificate.
@ref Criminal Code s 811.1(1) (src:17109-17110)
GIVEN `it is a prosecution for breach of a condition in a recognizance under section 810, 810.01, 810.011, 810.03, 810.1 or 810.2 that a defendant not consume drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate purports to be signed by an analyst` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate states that the analyst has analyzed a sample of a bodily substance and states the result of the analysis` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 811.1(1) the certificate is admissible in evidence` MEANS
    IF `it is a prosecution for breach of a condition in a recognizance under section 810, 810.01, 810.011, 810.03, 810.1 or 810.2 that a defendant not consume drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance`
       AND `the certificate purports to be signed by an analyst`
       AND `the certificate states that the analyst has analyzed a sample of a bodily substance and states the result of the analysis`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In a prosecution for breach of a condition ... a certificate purporting to be signed by an analyst that states ..."

@ref Criminal Code s 811.1(1) (src:17109-17110)
GIVEN `the certificate is admissible, by s 811.1(1) the certificate is admissible in evidence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 811.1(1) the certificate is proof of the statements contained in it without proof of the signature or official character` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the certificate is admissible, by s 811.1(1) the certificate is admissible in evidence` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND NOT `there is evidence to the contrary` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the certificate is admissible, by s 811.1(1) the certificate is admissible in evidence` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `there is evidence to the contrary` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the absence of evidence to the contrary, is proof of the statements"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the certificate is outside the subsection

-- 811.1(2) In this section, analyst has the same meaning as in section 320.11.
-- src:17111 | Definition of analyst
-- src:17112 | (2) In this section, analyst has the same meaning as in section 320.11.
@ref Criminal Code s 811.1(2) "analyst" (src:17111-17112)
GIVEN `s 320.11 the person is an analyst` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 811.1(2) analyst` MEANS
    `s 320.11 the person is an analyst`

-- 811.1(3) No certificate shall be admitted in evidence unless the party intending to produce it has, before the trial, given reasonable notice and a copy of the certificate to the party against whom it is to be produced.
-- src:17113 | Notice of intention to produce certificate
-- src:17114 | (3) No certificate shall be admitted in evidence unless the party intending to produce it has, before the trial, given reasonable notice and a copy of the certificate to the party against whom it is to be produced.
@ref Criminal Code s 811.1(3) (src:17113-17114)
GIVEN `the party intending to produce the certificate has, before the trial, given reasonable notice to the party against whom it is to be produced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party has, before the trial, given a copy of the certificate to the party against whom it is to be produced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 811.1(3) the certificate is barred from admission in evidence` MEANS
    IF `the party intending to produce the certificate has, before the trial, given reasonable notice to the party against whom it is to be produced`
       AND `the party has, before the trial, given a copy of the certificate to the party against whom it is to be produced`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the party intending to produce it has, before the trial, given reasonable notice and a copy of the certificate"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- 811.1(4) The party against whom a certificate of an analyst is produced may, with leave of the court, require the attendance of the analyst for cross-examination.
-- src:17115 | Requiring attendance of analyst
-- src:17116 | (4) The party against whom a certificate of an analyst is produced may, with leave of the court, require the attendance of the analyst for cross-examination.
@ref Criminal Code s 811.1(4) (src:17115-17116)
-- @name-test: flipped to NOTHING; gates "If a certificate of an analyst is produced against a party" and "with leave of the court" (fork F-811.1-4)
GIVEN `a certificate of an analyst is produced against the party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court gives leave` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 811.1(4) the party may require the attendance of the analyst for cross-examination` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a certificate of an analyst is produced against the party` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The party against whom a certificate of an analyst is produced"
        IF NOT `the court gives leave` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may, with leave of the court"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
